Our site does not display {language} yet. The translations are ready in glot, and the language switcher sends the code "{locale}" to the site (for example ?lang={locale}), but the site ignores it and stays in its default language. The site's code probably only accepts short codes such as "en" or "fr".

Two ways to fix it:
1. Accept "{locale}" wherever the site reads the language (a letters-only or length check rejects it).
2. Or tell me which code the site expects for {language}, and I will set it in glot (Settings, Locales).

